# Canonical author identity.
#
# One person, several name spellings and two addresses. The mapping normalizes
# what git reports while leaving every commit object untouched, so every SHA
# referenced anywhere still resolves.
#
# The left-hand side is the canonical form. Each right-hand side is a variant as
# it appears in the commits, and must stay exactly as written there or it stops
# mapping.
